{
    "background_story": "Dalia was a majestic Black Vulture, known to her kin as a member of the Coragyps genus. She soared through the skies of the American Southwest, her broad wings beating effortlessly as she scanned the landscape for carrion. Despite her reputation as a scavenger, Dalia was a noble creature, respected by her fellow birds for her sharp eyesight and fearless nature. She played a crucial role in the ecosystem, cleaning up carcasses and preventing the spread of disease. Dalia's intelligence and adaptability allowed her to thrive in a world filled with predators and competitors. Her distinctive black plumage glistened in the sunlight as she rode the thermals, a symbol of resilience and determination in the harsh yet beautiful desert landscape.",
